<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav June trade gap $110 mln v $124 mln in May.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav June trade gap $110 mln v $124 mln in May.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV TRADE	    JUNE	  MAY	  JUNE 96</p>
<p> Exports mln USD	    156	  171	     180</p>
<p> Imports			266	  295	     373</p>
<p> Balance		     -110	 -124	    -193</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE FIGURES (JANUARY TO JUNE)</p>
<p> Exports mln USD	  1,028	  862	     800</p>
<p> Imports		    2,112	1,709	   1,735</p>
<p> Balance		   -1,084	 -847	    -935</p>
<p>NOTES -- June year-on-year exports dropped 13.1 percent and imports dropped 28.6 percent on June 1996, the report said.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-June exports were 28.5 percent up, and imports 21.7 percent up on the same six-month period last year.</p>
<p>Yugoslavia's 1996 trade gap stood at $2.26 billion, with exports worth around $1.842 and imports $4.102 billion.</p>
<p>Data refers to the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 311 4305</p>
